# -*- mode:org; coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: layoutlist-returns-model -- (layoutlist) is a stub returning ("Model"); the vendors list the paper layouts only
#+STATUS: DONE
#+PRIORITY: P3
#+TYPE: divergence
#+DEPENDS: -
#+DATE: 2026-10-04

* Observed

builtin-layoutlist (autolisp-builtins-core/source/api.lisp) returns
("Model") whatever the drawing. The AutoLISP reference: LAYOUTLIST "Returns
a list of all paper space layouts in the current drawing" -- Model is not
one; EPUREE writes (cons "Model" (layoutlist)) for that reason
(src/comu.lsp, epuree:delete-layouts-by-name-list), so under clautolisp it
sees "Model" twice.

Found while implementing Document.Layouts (com-application-object-
properties, 2.2.179), which lists Layout1 and Model from the drawing.

* To do

Probe (layoutlist) on both vendors (a fresh drawing: AutoCAD headless can
answer, it is not COM); then derive it from the host's layout blocks, the
same source as Document.Layouts (a host protocol call: builtins-core cannot
see cador's tables).

* Measured and done (2026-10-05, clautolisp 2.2.183)

probe-triage3, French templates: never "Model". AutoCAD 2022 (job
16931597043): ("Présentation1" "Présentation2"), after LAYOUT New
ProbeLayout ("ProbeLayout" "Présentation1" "Présentation2") -- sorted by
name. BricsCAD V25 Windows / V26 macOS (jobs 16931597047 / 16931597044): the
same two, then ProbeLayout last -- tab order. CTAB "Model" on all.
Implemented: host-layout-names (autolisp-host protocol; cador: the paper
layout blocks, *Paper_Space = "Layout1"), sorted under the AutoCAD dialects.
Spec: LAYOUTLIST, Measured + clautolisp.
